Hi all,

This is the second part of vnode table full post. Basically to summarize
the first part, I was saying that we were having system crashes and the
reported error "vnode table full", "simple lock owned". I also said that
this happened only after we had applied october 96 digital patches.

Since I posted the first  message we have found some answer :
- Apparently the bug came from our application : we have an application
that control/supervise the trains of the HK metro. It runs 24 hours a day
and we generate a lot of application logs. These logs tend to grow big so
we have defined a maximum size after which the log is erased and we open it
again. The problem is that we do not close the log files, we just open it
again. It means that every time we open it again we get a new file id which
is eating a vnode table entry. Thus the vnode table fills up ... and the
machine crashes ...

However I still have two questions for which I'd like to find an answer :

1) As I told you in my previous mail (have I ?) the crash problem only
appeared after we installed october 96 set of Digital Patches. But the
problem existed a long time before in our application. Our number of logs
having not changed significantly it seems that the patches changed
something in the way the vnode table is managed. This is why I'd like to
know. Why the problem is more frequent now ?

For information, the patches we installed are the 31/10/96 patche set
