Adrian Burd wrote:

> We are running a network of Dec Alpha 3000's running OSF/1 v3.2
> and would like to attach an Iomega Jaz drive to one of the machines.

I have made the Jaz drive work with me system.  

scu see's the device, however I have not explored all of the scu options
(eject works fine).  To make the drive work, I had to create an entry in
the /etc/disktab file.  The following is the entry I use (I found this
on the web some where)

jaz-single|IOMEGA Jaz 1GB drive:\
        :ty=winchester:dt=SCSI:ns#3217:nt#1:nc#650:\
        :oa#0:pa#2091050:ba#8192:fa#1024: \
        :oc#0:pc#2091050:bc#8192:fc#1024:

With this entry one can issue the command

newfs /dev/rz?c jaz-single 

where ? is the SCSI # of the jaz drive.  I do not think FAT formated
disks are supported at all under OSF/1 3.2.  I have to mount and umount
the drive when ever I insert or eject a disk.  NOTE you will hang the
system completely if you eject the disk while it is mounted and then try
to access the disk.

e.g.
mount /dev/rz2c /jaz
**eject disk
ls /jaz
**hang system

Derek



