Dilip Dasilva wrote:
> 
>  Hi,
> 
>  I am trying to compile a program that uses threads on Dec Unix 4.0B
>  that compiled without a problem on Dec Unix 3.2.
> 
>  It uses posix threads so I have the following include file
> 
>    #include <pthread.h>
> 
>  The problem is that these files are different between 4.0B and 3.2.
>  The 4.0B file does not contain the definitions for pthread_startroutine_t
>  and pthread__addr_t .  These definitions are included in
>  /usr/include/pthread_exc.h. I noticed that there are two pthread.h
>  include files - one in /usr/include/pthread.h and the other in
>  /usr/include/dce/pthread.h . On 3.2 one of these files was
>  a linked to the other.
> 
>   Does anyone know which include files I need to get my program to
>   compile on 4.0B.
> 
>  Thanks, Dilip

3.2 uses Posix threads that are based on the draft for the Posix threads
standard. Dec Unix 4.0 uses a Pthread library that is based on the final
Posix thread standard. Unfortunately, there are a number of differences
between the draft and the final standard, and you will probably have to
make a number of changes in your thread handling code.

For a discussion of the differences between the draft and final standard
see e.g. "Pthreads Programming" by Bradford Nichols e.a., O'reilly.
(http://www.ora.com/catalog/pthread/noframes.html)

Peter

