Kamal Kishore Mantri wrote:
> 
> Hi,
>         I want to intialize some global data & acquire few
> system resources(mutexes, shared memory .. etc) when shared
> library is loaded. Similiarly these resouces need to released
> when shared library is unloaded. Can anybody suggest me a way
> of doing this in Digital UNIX 4.0. In HP-UX , it could have
> been done with +I_INITIALIZER flag in ld.
> 

Kamal,

Please take a look at the ld(1) man page, specifically, this section:

"Symbol names that start with __init_ and __fini_ have special meaning to
the linker.  All routines that start with __init_ are treated, by default,
as initialization routines.  These are routines that are called without an
argument when the file that contains them is loaded or when the program
that contains them is started.  All routines that start with __fini_ are
treated by default as termination routines, which are routines that are
called without an argument when the file that contains them is unloaded or
when the program that contains them exits."

This sounds exactly like what you want, yes?   If you cannot rename
the routines, you may also want to look at the -init and -fini
linker options, which let you name symbols that you wish to be
treated as init or fini routines.

Hope this helps...

Craig

