> can
> get it to boot the NT 4.0 floppy that the rest of the setup is just
> like any other NT installation??
>
> I'd appreciate any assistance.

  Robert,
You don't need to boot it up from a floppy. In the SRM console, set the
OS type to WindowsNT. The power it down. When the power comes back up,
you will be in the ARC console. The ARC console has an argument to
install Windows NT. You can also run a program directly from the Windows
NT CD ROM. There is a program on the NT CD-ROM, arcinst.exe which allows
you to partition and format the NT partitions. Another difference
between Intel and Digital here is that the boot partition must bne FAT.
Normally, we make the boot partition 4-6MB. Then set up the rest as NTFS
partitions. BTW: The ARC console does contain the BIOS emulation where
the SRM does not. Also, being a bit disjointed today, the standard WNT
CD-ROM contains both the Intel and Alpha NT versions.

